sheng — register-resident refutation sieves for regex
Copyright 2026 The Billy Company

This product includes software developed at The Billy Company
(https://billylives.com/).

No third-party source or data is bundled here. The crate depends on memchr
through the registry, and on regex-automata under its default features, and both
keep their own notices; nothing is vendored into this tree.

The idea and the kernel are not original to this package, and the README
credits them where they are used: the substitution property and its lattice
are Hartmanis & Stearns (1966); the register-resident DFA is Geoff Langdale's
Sheng (2018), which ships in Hyperscan; the enumerative parallelization is
Mytkowicz, Musuvathi & Schulte (ASPLOS 2014); the nibble set classifier is
Wojciech Muła's SIMDized byte lookup (2018), which ships in Hyperscan as
shufti. No code was copied from any of them.
